# Tests must pass before feature complete

Do **not** call a feature, bugfix, or change set complete until the relevant test pack has been **executed locally (or in CI) and passed**.

## Required gate

Before stating work is done, run and confirm green the **full test pack** via `./build.ps1` (or `dotnet test` on the test project with no filter).

Narrow with `-TestFilter` / `--filter` only when the change is clearly isolated **and** you still cover every layer that could regress (Unit / Integration / EndToEnd namespaces).

## What “complete” means

- ❌ Do not say “done”, “fixed”, or “feature complete” based only on reasoning, partial tests, or a prior green run from before the latest edits.
- ✅ Re-run after the final code change. Fix failures before declaring complete.
- If Docker/Testcontainers are unavailable for integration/E2E, say so explicitly and do not claim full completion.

## Examples

```text
# ❌ BAD
Implemented serialization. Feature complete.

# ✅ GOOD
Implemented serialization. Ran unit + integration (pass). E2E WorldTop100 pass. Feature complete.
```
